course: dictionary
lesson: 12705
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which one is meant by reading the words around it. This is context again: the clues show which meaning fits.
explain: «Mia cuddled her dolly before bed.» Here a dolly is a child's toy, a doll. Cuddled and bed are clues, because children cuddle toys at bedtime. Put the meaning in the sentence and check it makes sense.
explain: «The movers slid the piano onto a dolly and wheeled it out.» This dolly is a low platform with wheels, used to move something heavy. Slid, wheeled and piano are the clues. The same word can also mean a very easy catch in cricket.
fact: A dolly is a child's word for a doll.
fact: A dolly can also be a small low platform with wheels, used to move heavy things or to move a film camera smoothly.
fact: In cricket, a dolly or dolly catch is a very easy catch.
fact: «Dolly mixtures» are a UK sweet, and a «rag dolly» is a doll made of cloth.
fact: Old UK slang «dolly bird» was a rude-ish word for a pretty young woman; it is not polite to use it now.
exercise: «Mia cuddled her dolly before bed.» What does dolly mean here? | A very easy catch in cricket | A sweet you buy in a shop | *A child's doll | A low platform with wheels
exercise: «The movers slid the piano onto a dolly.» What is a dolly here? | *A low platform with wheels for moving heavy things | A child's toy | A cricket catch | A pretty young woman
exercise: The crowd shouted, «Easy dolly!» as the fielder caught the ball. What does dolly mean? | *A very easy catch | A kind of sweet | A soft toy | A camera with wheels
test: «The camera moved smoothly along the track on a dolly.» What does dolly mean here? | A doll for playing with | A rude word for a young woman | *A small platform with wheels | A very easy catch
test: Which phrase means a very easy catch in cricket? | *dolly catch | rag dolly | camera dolly | dolly mixtures
exam: Which meaning of dolly is old slang and not polite to use now? | A very easy catch | A low platform with wheels | *A rude-ish old word for a pretty young woman | A child's doll
